  "answer": "We prefer a convex mirror as a rear-view mirror in vehicles because it provides a wider field of view compared to a plane mirror. This is due to the way light reflects off a convex surface. When light rays from an object strike a convex mirror, they diverge (spread out) after reflection. This divergence allows the mirror to capture a larger area behind the vehicle, making it easier for the driver to see more of the surroundings. Additionally, the image formed by a convex mirror is always virtual, upright, and smaller than the actual object, which helps in reducing the risk of blind spots.",
